<!-- Lessons: the two slots of the quote layout, and the deck's only **inverted slide**. `<slide invert>`
     swaps bg ↔ fg on this slide alone — one light slide in the middle of a dark deck says "remember just
     this sentence". The source's `color="fg"` stays as is; in PPTX it is a color-map override, so the
     theme colors move the slide. -->
<slide id="lessons" layout="quote" invert enter="rise">
  <blockquote slot="quote" size="48" color="fg">A cache is not an availability tool. It is only a cache
  if you can survive the load the moment it is gone.</blockquote>
  <text slot="attribution" role="caption" color="muted" align="end">— the one sentence we agreed on</text>
  <note>This sentence goes at the top of the cache design review checklist.</note>
</slide>
